(7460791, 1182773, 103142, '<td valign="top">I adore the POV on this one. What a wonderful spot! It just makes me want to go there and explore. I want to walk that path and sit on the rocks with a good book.  Thanks for drawing me in. When can I come visit?</td>', 'I adore the POV on this one. What a wonderful spot! It just makes me want to go there and explore. I want to walk that path and sit on the rocks with a good book.  Thanks for drawing me in. When can I come visit?', '2016-06-20 10:42:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(7460797, 1182781, 104230, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vawendy:</b></div><hr/><i> What an absolutely gorgeous field! Huge congrats on HM! How do you like Bear''s camera? <br/> <br/>Dizziness is such an awful feeling -- I''m so glad you''re feeling better! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you, Wendy. I loved this field and just had to stop for it. Robert and I both shoot with Sony mirrorless cameras now, and the alpha 7 and 7R are the same body and we set them up the same, so it''s a pretty seamless transition from one to the other. The main difference is that while we bought two 24-70 mm lenses we share a wide angle and a 70-200 lens and the wide angle is usually "housed" in Robert''s camera bag !!</td>', 'Originally posted by vawendy: What an absolutely gorgeous field! Huge congrats on HM! How do you like Bear''s camera?  Dizziness is such an awful feeling -- I''m so glad you''re feeling better!   Thank you, Wendy. I loved this field and just had to stop for it. Robert and I both shoot with Sony mirrorless cameras now, and the alpha 7 and 7R are the same body and we set them up the same, so it''s a pretty seamless transition from one to the other. The main difference is that while we bought two 24-70 mm lenses we share a wide angle and a 70-200 lens and the wide angle is usually "housed" in Robert''s camera bag !!', '2016-06-20 11:01:23.000000', NULL, 0),
